From: Sidharth Renukadevi <srenukad@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:30:04
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:PROTOCOL:HOSTAPD: AP MLD: prevent NULL drv_priv dereference during interface reconfiguration

AP MLD radio reconfiguration can trigger a reload cascade across
partner interfaces within the same MLD group. During this sequence,
a partner interface teardown may clear drv_priv for AP MLD member
BSSes through hostapd_cleanup_driver(), even when other links in the
MLD group remain active.

Subsequent interface reinitialization may reuse the shared AP MLD
context and inherit a NULL drv_priv from the group's reference BSS.
The NULL pointer is later passed to driver callbacks during
hostapd_driver_init(), resulting in a crash when
wpa_driver_nl80211_get_capa() dereferences the driver private context.

The failure is observed during AP MLD radio disable/enable sequences,
where cross-interface reload processing can temporarily leave AP MLD
link state inconsistent while interfaces are being rebuilt.

Fix this by:

  * Validating the shared AP MLD driver's drv_priv before propagating
    it to a non-primary AP MLD link during setup. If drv_priv is not
    available, abort link initialization and report a setup failure
    instead of invoking driver callbacks with a NULL context.

  * Avoiding premature drv_priv invalidation for active AP MLD member
    BSSes during interface cleanup when the MLD group still contains
    remaining references. This prevents transient teardown operations
    from removing driver context that may still be required by sibling
    links during reconfiguration.

With these changes, AP MLD reconfiguration failures are handled
gracefully and no longer result in a NULL pointer dereference in the
nl80211 driver capability path.

Patch-dependency: None

Signed-off-by: Sidharth Renukadevi <srenukad@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -179,6 +179,16 @@
 		h_hapd = hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd);
 	}
 
+	if (h_hapd && !h_hapd->drv_priv) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
+			   "MLD: first-link BSS %s of AP MLD has no driver "
+			   "context (drv_priv is NULL); aborting driver "
+			   "init of link %d (%s)",
+			   h_hapd->conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+			   hapd->conf->iface);
+		return -1;
+	}
+
 	if (h_hapd) {
 		hapd->drv_priv = h_hapd->drv_priv;
 		hapd->interface_added = h_hapd->interface_added;

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1957,6 +1957,16 @@
 			struct hostapd_data *h_hapd;
 
 			h_hapd = hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd);
+			if (h_hapd && !h_hapd->drv_priv) {
+				wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
+					   "MLD: first-link BSS %s of AP MLD "
+					   "has no driver context (drv_priv "
+					   "is NULL); aborting setup of link "
+					   "%d (%s)",
+					   h_hapd->conf->iface,
+					   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
+				return -1;
+			}
 			if (h_hapd) {
 				hapd->drv_priv = h_hapd->drv_priv;
 				hapd->interface_added = h_hapd->interface_added;
@@ -4538,12 +4548,20 @@
 		return;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
-	if (!driver->is_drv_shared ||
-	    !driver->is_drv_shared(drv_priv, iface->bss[0]->mld_link_id)) {
-		driver->hapd_deinit(drv_priv);
-		hostapd_mld_interface_freed(iface->bss[0]);
-		iface->bss[0]->drv_priv = NULL;
-		return;
+	{
+		struct hostapd_data *bss0 = iface->bss[0];
+		bool mld_has_other_members = bss0->conf->mld_ap && bss0->mld &&
+			bss0->mld->refcount > 1;
+
+		/* Keep the shared driver context while other MLD members exist. */
+		if ((!driver->is_drv_shared ||
+		     !driver->is_drv_shared(drv_priv, bss0->mld_link_id)) &&
+		    !mld_has_other_members) {
+			driver->hapd_deinit(drv_priv);
+			hostapd_mld_interface_freed(bss0);
+			bss0->drv_priv = NULL;
+			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (iface->bss[0]->conf->mld_ap) {
